<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10959" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνώνῠμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		(from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνυμα,</span>
		
			Aeol.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνομα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without name,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ μὲν γάρ τις πάμπαν ἀ. ἐστ᾽
					ἀνθρώπων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.552
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Εὐρώπη . . ἦν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.45
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεαί</span> i.e. the Furies, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				944
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὅρκου πάϊς ἐστὶν ἀ.</span>
			Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.86
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				60a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1107b2
			</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Po.</u>
				1447b9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Tz.
				<u>Diff. Poet.</u>
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>anonymous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήνυσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					13.22
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				66.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>not to be named, unspeakable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				50(26).8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>difficult to name,</i> in 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EE</u>
				1221a40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>in Mete.</u>
				197.23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως</span>
			<i>without mentioning a name,</i> Men.Rh.<i><span class="en">
				p.391
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>nameless, inglorious,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					1.82
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ πατρὶς οὐκ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνομα ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					854
				</span></i>
			; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				377
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				721c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἄδοξοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					8.66
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				6.14
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					5.160
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
